Package: BadgerInfeR
Type: Package
Title: Badger Diagnostic HMM Inference via a Standalone Binary
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Arthur", "Newbury", email = "a.r.newbury@exeter.ac.uk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: In-house interface to the badger diagnostic Hidden Markov Model,
    wrapping the trimmed standalone 'test2inf' executable instead of a Julia
    session. Latent infection status is inferred on a regular time grid from
    imperfect test results, with sensitivity and specificity either fixed at
    published values or estimated, and culture specificity optionally pinned
    to one. Deliberately restricted to the four model variants used in the
    project's current comparison. Requires no Julia and no R-side compilation
    on the target machine.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Imports:
    parallel,
    stats,
    tools,
    utils
Suggests:
    digest,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: the test2inf binary (see ?badger_binary)
